## N3 — THE CLASSIFICATION, and it is this block's headline **positive**

### The closed statement

> **`D` is positive definite for some choice of the four duality parameters at
> a compatible point IF AND ONLY IF**
>
> ```text
> gamma0 < 1/2   when pi0 = +1     (any gamma0 < 1 when pi0 = -1),
> ```
>
> **AND, independently,**
>
> ```text
> gamma1 < 1/2   when pi1 = +1     (any gamma1 < 1 when pi1 = -1).
> ```

**Necessity** is `N2`: the four degree blocks are principal submatrices and
contain none of the free parameters, so blocks-PD is necessary and no duality
choice can rescue a failing block. **Sufficiency** is the degree-diagonal
representative: at `a = b = c = d = 0` the matrix **is** the direct sum of the
four blocks. The two halves close on each other exactly, which is why this is a
theorem about the region rather than a report about points.

Per class, on the two-parameter magnitude base:

| class `(pi0, pi1)` | PD region |
| :---: | --- |
| `(+1, +1)` | `[0, 1/2) × [0, 1/2)` |
| `(+1, -1)` | `[0, 1/2) × [0, 1)` |
| `(-1, +1)` | `[0, 1) × [0, 1/2)` |
| `(-1, -1)` | `[0, 1)^2` — the **whole** base |

**EVERY GAUGE CLASS CARRIES A TWO-PARAMETER CURVED POSITIVE DEFINITE FAMILY.**

### And that refutes the natural extension

Block 209 proved its **one** exhibited curved point was never a geometry, and
scoped the conclusion to the checked branches. The sentence one would naturally
have written next — *literal gluing plus positivity admits exactly the flat
cell* — is **false**. It is false in every gauge class, including the all-plus
one, and it is false at small shear where nothing exotic is happening.

**BLOCK 209 DID NOT WRITE THAT SENTENCE.** Its scoping was exact, and that is
the difference between a completed block and a corrected one.

### The grid, which confirms and does not prove

```text
32 exact solves   =   8 rational magnitude points  x  4 gauge classes,
full 8 x 8 leading principal minors at the degree-diagonal representative,
verdicts agree with the region formula at EVERY point,
census   (+,+) 3/8,   (+,-) 3/8,   (-,+) 3/8,   (-,-) 8/8      =  17 / 32,
at every non-PD point the parameter-free deg-1 or deg-2 DETERMINANT is <= 0.
```

The last line is the important one. **The killer is never a duality-dependent
minor**; it is always a determinant of a parameter-free principal block, which
is why one sign test closes every duality choice at once. Which minor kills
which branch is fully determined: `det(v1 M1) = v1^3 (1 + g0)^2 (1 - 2 g0)` on
the positive-orientation side of offset 0, `det(M2/v0)` likewise for offset 1,
and `D00 = v0 > 0` and `D77 = 1/v1 > 0` never bind on the positive-volume
family. The negative-volume mirror is compatible and dies at the **first** minor.

